 235++89BC
 236++89BC                          ; Test vector template.
 237++89BC                          ;
 238++89BC                          ; Each test consists of the following:
 239++89BC                          ; - Bitmask of which of the modified flags are officially documented.
 240++89BC                          ; - Three test vectors - base test vector, counter vector and shifter vector.
 241++89BC                          ; - The CRCs for each of the available test variants.
 242++89BC                          ; - Test name.
 243++89BC                          ; - Type of test pre-check, if any.
 244++89BC                          ;
 245++89BC                          ; The base test vectors specifies the instruction(s) to execute,
 246++89BC                          ; the initial value of the memory operand, and the initial
 247++89BC                          ; values of the Z80 registers.
 248++89BC                          ;
 249++89BC                          ; The counter vector specifies which combinations of bits shall
 250++89BC                          ; be toggled in the base test vectors. The test vector is
 251++89BC                          ; executed once for each possible combination.
 252++89BC                          ;
 253++89BC                          ; The shifter vector specifies which bits shall be toggled in
 254++89BC                          ; the test vector in sequence. After all the initial counter
 255++89BC                          ; combinations were executed, the whole process is repeated, but
 256++89BC                          ; now also toggling one of the specified shifter bits at a time.
 257++89BC                          ;
 258++89BC                          ; The pre-check byte specifies if the test should be skipped and under what condition.
 259++89BC                          ; Note that it is seldom needed so most often I abuse the flags byte of the following test instead.
 260++89BC
 261++89BC                          if 0
